From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:38:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: power modules with a pwrseq up from the rescan
 work

mmc_start_host() powers the card up in the host's probe, and with it
waits out the pwrseq's post-power-on delay (200 ms for the RG35XX's
RTL8821CS). The root mount waits for all probes, so that delay held it
up. With MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP the first rescan powers it up.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 0e1912bf9..020fbabcd 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1465,6 +1465,14 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	/* TODO: This driver doesn't support HS400 mode yet */
 	mmc->caps2 &= ~MMC_CAP2_HS400;
 
+	/*
+	 * Power an SDIO module up from the rescan work, not here: its pwrseq
+	 * delay (200 ms for some Wi-Fi modules) would hold up the probe, and
+	 * with it the root mount, which waits for all probes.
+	 */
+	if (mmc->pwrseq)
+		mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP;
+
 	ret = sunxi_mmc_init_host(host);
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_free_dma;
